  "final": "Implemented the `clamp` function and extended the public checks.\n\n**Changes**\n\n- `src/numbers.py`\n  - Added `clamp(value, lower, upper)`:\n    - Returns `lower` if `value < lower`\n    - Returns `upper` if `value > upper`\n    - Otherwise returns `value` unchanged (bounds are inclusive)\n    - Raises `ValueError` when `lower > upper`\n  - Preserved `add` exactly as before.\n\n- `checks/public.py`\n  - Kept the existing `add(2, 3) == 5` assertion.\n  - Added checks for value-inside-range, below-lower, above-upper, both inclusive boundaries, a degenerate `lower == upper` case, negative floats, and a `ValueError` case for `lower > upper`.\n\n**Verification**\n\nRan `cd /workspace && python3 checks/public.py` → `public checks passed` (exit code 0). No files outside `src/` and `checks/` were modified.",
